Android's cRPathFollowGoldy::Traverse (0004d70c) applies a path's heading only when
one is installed (0004ddb4), so a path without one keeps its own roll and a turnover
rolls the camera; its side exit (0004ddfc) has no hover guard, so the snail leaves a
path sideways with the jetpack on. Its cRCameraman::AI (00071248) lifts the camera
linearly to 0.55 along BuildSBend's own kind, 0x12 (000717e8), where the hills get
the bump, and off a lift path it eases the lift out by 0.98 a tick (000713c0)
instead of dropping it. The shell's S-bends (extras_paths.cpp) carry that kind.

